In the terminal if you were to run the command foo.txt | cat the terminal outputs the quinnoldland@MacBook-Pro-3 ~ % foo.txt | cat
zsh: command not found: foo.txt

In our code we implemented a process that first reads foo.txt and pipes the output to cat. The reason we implemented this is because we needed to satisfy the flow file in the project description here: 

node=read_file
command=cat

file=input_file
name=result.txt

node=word_count
command=wc

pipe=read_pipe
from=input_file
to=read_file

pipe=process_pipe
from=read_pipe
to=word_count

The terminal equivalent to this is result.txt | cat | wc which would be invalid which is why we made this assumption
